.TH GXWI-SERVER 8 2026-10-19 "Peios gxwi 0.0.7"
.SH NAME
gxwi-server \- serve browser traffic under a restricted GXWI token
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gxwi-server
.BI --listener-fd " fd"
.BI --channel-fd " fd"
.BI --overlay-fd " fd"
.BI --tls-fd " fd"
.RB [ --unrestricted ]
.RB [ --logon-name " name" ]
.RB [ --logon-notice " paragraph" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gxwi-server
is the network-facing worker started by
.BR gxwid (8).
The daemon supplies open descriptors and an initial certificate before the worker accepts browser traffic.
Do not start the worker directly.
.PP
The worker relays authenticated requests to session sockets, keeps GXWI cookies out of application requests, and prevents application responses from replacing those cookies.
It also routes machine overlays and isolated application origins.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --channel-fd " fd"
Inherited control channel to gxwid.
.TP
.BI --listener-fd " fd"
Inherited network listening socket.
.TP
.BI --logon-name " name"
Plain-text public machine label supplied by the daemon.
.TP
.BI --logon-notice " paragraph"
Plain-text public notice paragraph.
The option can be repeated in display order.
.TP
.BI --overlay-fd " fd"
Inherited overlay-state channel.
.TP
.BI --tls-fd " fd"
Inherited channel carrying the initial key and certificate and later certificate replacements.
.TP
.B --unrestricted
Skip the native sandbox probe for development runs controlled by gxwid.
.SH SECURITY
Normal execution requires the restricted token supplied by gxwid.
The worker refuses normal startup if it can list the filesystem root.
The probe is a startup check, not a replacement for the kernel's access checks.
TLS keys arrive on a private channel rather than through direct key-file access.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 1
Required descriptors, initial certificate, overlay state, sandbox checks, or service startup failed.
Otherwise the worker serves until stopped or its service loop ends.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gxwid (8)
